    ci(build): give every packaging leg a rasterizer, and refuse unsafe copies
    
    Follow-up to the branding fix, so the shipped icons are actually refreshed on all
    three install targets, not only on Linux:
    
    • scripts/refresh-brand-icons.mjs only copies raw upload bytes when they really
      are a SQUARE PNG (IHDR parsed inline — no new dependency), and only into the
      targets whose consumer resizes: the manifest promises image/png, Android wants
      exact density dims, iOS forbids alpha and electron-builder can only shrink, so
      a JPEG or a 600×300 wordmark is now refused with an actionable warning instead
      of being renamed into an installer icon. A 512 slot additionally requires a
      source of at least 512px.
    • .github/workflows/build-desktop.yml installs ImageMagick on the Windows and
      macOS legs (choco / brew, PATH re-exported because a job's environment is fixed
      at job start); ubuntu-latest already ships it. Both steps are
      continue-on-error: a failed install degrades that build's branding, it must
      never fail a release.
    
    Verified the three fallback paths against fixtures (square PNG → 3 copies,
    non-square → nothing, JPEG → nothing), and with ImageMagick present a 600×600
    JPEG still refreshes all 37 files. npm test 541 pass.
    
    Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/.github/workflows/build-desktop.yml b/.github/workflows/build-desktop.yml
index 8ac7e27..7d13b89 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/build-desktop.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/build-desktop.yml
@@ -54,6 +54,32 @@ jobs:
       - name: Type-check
         run: npm run typecheck
 
+      # Branding is part of the shipped artwork. scripts/refresh-brand-icons.mjs
+      # (run by build:web below) rasterizes the administrator's PUBLISHED logo into
+      # public/icon-512.png, build/icons — which is what becomes the Windows .ico and
+      # the Linux hicolor set — the Android mipmap buckets and the iOS AppIcon.
+      # Without a rasterizer the script degrades to a warning and the committed
+      # artwork ships, so this install step is a quality-of-build improvement, never
+      # a requirement: continue-on-error keeps branding from breaking packaging.
+      - name: Ensure ImageMagick (brand icon refresh)
+        if: matrix.os == 'ubuntu-latest'
+        continue-on-error: true
+        run: |
+          if command -v convert >/dev/null 2>&1; then echo "ImageMagick present"; exit 0; fi
+          sudo apt-get update -qq && sudo apt-get install -y -qq imagemagick
+
+      - name: Ensure ImageMagick (brand icon refresh)
+        if: matrix.os == 'windows-latest'
+        continue-on-error: true
+        shell: pwsh
+        run: |
+          if (Get-Command convert -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue) { "ImageMagick present"; exit 0 }
+          choco install imagemagick --no-progress -y
+          # choco updates the machine PATH, which this job's later steps do not
+          # inherit — export the directory ourselves.
+          $dir = Get-ChildItem 'C:\Program Files\ImageMagick-*' -Directory | Sort-Object Name -Descending | Select-Object -First 1
+          if ($dir) { $dir.FullName | Out-File -FilePath $env:GITHUB_PATH -Encoding ascii -Append }
+
       - name: Build renderer (web build)
         run: npm run build:web
 
